  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PCAsia 2023-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PCAsia 2023-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It is aimed that by 2030, PCAsia contributes to an improvement in the performance of the target Parliaments  Cambodia, Lao PDR, Myanmar (currently suspended) and ASEAN Inter- Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA)- by helping to strengthen the capacity of parliamentary staff, and by increasing the intensity of technical exchanges and experience-sharing among their regional peers. There are three indicators as follow: 1) Parliamentary staff provide more effective support to Parliamentarians to perform legislative review, representation and oversight. 2) Parliamentarians perform their core functions of legislation, representation and oversight more effectively. 3) Stakeholders are increasingly satisfied with parliamentary performance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r projektet &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra och utveckla en rad PCAsia-aktiviteter relaterade till kapacitetsutvecklingen av ASEAN:s interparlamentariska f&#xf6;rsamlings (AIPA) medlemsparlament om parlamentariskt arbete. Detta bidrar ocks&#xe5; till en f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttring av parlamentens prestationer i Sydostasien genom att bidra till att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos parlamentarisk personal och genom att &#xf6;ka intensiteten i tekniskt utbyte och erfarenhetsutbyte mellan deras regionala och internationella kamrater.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Project is to improve and develop a range of PCAsia activities related to the capacity development of the ASEAN Inter-parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) Member Parliaments on parliamentary works. This also contributes to an improvement in the performance of the Parliaments in South East Asia by helping to strengthen the capacity of parliamentary staff, and by increasing the intensity of technical exchanges and experience-sharing among their regional and international peers.</narrative>
  </description>
